uarch provides C++26 CMake targets:

    find_package(uarch CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE uarch::uarch)

uarch::uarch is the hosted umbrella over uarch::primitives (uarch::tiers,
uarch::core, uarch::arch) and uarch::detect (static libuarch_detect.a).
uarch::primitives (alias uarch::freestanding) is the runtime-free header-only
primitives umbrella (<uarch/primitives.hpp>).

A working C++26 reflection compiler is required. The installed configuration
checks structural annotations, expansion statements and the other upstream
reflection requirements; this check is deliberately retained. Clang requires
its reflection-enabled build with libc++; Clang with libstdc++ is unsupported
and fails the upstream reflection probe. GCC 16 with -freflection is the verified
configuration. The existing clang-glibc libstdc++ wrapper is not supported.
The imported targets propagate the appropriate reflection options.

Headers: <uarch/uarch.hpp> and <uarch/detect/detect.hpp>.
Detection audits the caller's existing affinity domain and never changes it;
see the upstream detection policy for multi-CPU evidence requirements.
